; equality_integer_model: EQUALITY on an integer {0, 1, 2} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; EQUALITY writes the penalty for x0 + x1 = 1, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which fails for spin variables
; and for integer variables with k > 2. The check follows the declared domain
; (only a model whose domain is binary passes), so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has EQUALITY raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 3, 4 variables
VECI r1          ; indices [0, 1]
PUSH 0
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r1
VECI r2          ; coeffs [1, 1]
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 1           ; target
PUSH 2           ; penalty
EQUALITY r0 r1 r2
HALT
